From 93ce95ddbedfc9914ef9579d07db3b5d80a7d06d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 17:34:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix security & correctness issues from code review
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Security / correctness:
- IDOR: reorder endpoints (sections/lessons/questions) now constrain
  updateMany to the verified parent (courseId/sectionId/quizId), so an
  instructor can no longer overwrite the order of records they don't own.
- Auth in API routes: add throwing guards (requireApi*) + authErrorResponse
  so unauthorized requests return 401/403/404 instead of a 500 swallowed
  from next/navigation redirect(). Page guards keep redirect behavior.
- Password reset now actually revokes sessions: add User.passwordChangedAt,
  set it on reset, and invalidate older JWTs in the NextAuth jwt callback
  (the no-op session.deleteMany did nothing under JWT strategy).
- Normalize email to lowercase on register, credentials login and
  forgot-password to match mobile login (prevents duplicate accounts and
  case-mismatch login failures).
- Quiz taker: guard against double-submit on timer auto-submit, submit the
  latest answers via ref (no stale closure), and track attempts in-session
  so the retake button respects maxAttempts.
- Mux upload: delete the previous asset before replacing to avoid orphaned
  assets and lingering signed playback IDs.
- /api/courses: validate/clamp limit & offset to avoid slice(offset, NaN).

Cleanup:
- Remove dead code: unused quiz-grading.ts duplicate engine, mux
  getStreamUrl and mapMuxStatus.

Note: tsc/tests not run — npm registry unreachable in this environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RjHCL9KBp42djY9211LvCv
